  "interpretation_note": "The flat-vs-steep plateau spring lag (+3.53 d raw, +3.15 d well-drained, +2.62 d unharvested) is robust across all 25 spatial block-grid alignments at both 1 km and 2 km scales. However, October mARI is grid-alignment-sensitive at 2 km clustering, and modeled soil layers (POLARIS/gNATSGO) cannot prove absence of fine-scale edaphic effects without species-level basal-area plots; therefore, evidence is consistent with upland oak guild turnover rather than definitive species-level proof."
